   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜だけ: only",
     "texto": [
      "**だけ** limits the element before it: **パン だけ たべます** (I only eat bread). It can go with an affirmative or a negative sentence, depending on what you want to say; it doesn't always need an affirmative verb."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜ばかり and 〜しか",
     "texto": [
      "**ばかり** usually expresses that there is a lot of something or that it keeps happening: **ゲーム ばかり して います** (I do nothing but play games). **しか** means \"only\" and needs a negative form: **パン しか ありません** (there's nothing but bread). Don't confuse **ばかり** with **〜た ばかり** (\"have just\")."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
